                <pb facs="0604" n="484" xml:id="pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.105/372: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-20T12:00:00-05:00">June 20,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 11:03 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>66. Referring to my telegram No. 61, June 18, the final report of the Board of
                    Investigation completely cleared Aarons of the charges against him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
